# Product / UX standing preferences

- Use open source (or a reputable free tier of an OSS product) before building commodity systems: analytics, charts, email, CMS, search, observability.
- Custom code is for FindMyInvite-specific invitation experience, not Mixpanel clones.
- Keep `/akay` unlinked from public pages if it remains.
- Do not store analytics events in the guest invitations database.
- Form/Editor **Create** opens Razorpay with no host sign-in. A browser draft token is enough; the public guest page is created only after a captured payment, then a preview + copy-link dialog. If Create is tapped again after a captured payment (tab close, retry), skip a second checkout and publish the page. Sign in stays available for My Templates. Forgot password is backlog; do not build it until Ashok asks.
- Homepage is an Instamart-style e-invite shop, not a cream marketing landing. No gold FindMyInvite header on `/`, `/templates`, or `/form`. First paint: white **Categories** with shop-by-store arches and occasion/tradition/collection/setting tiles. Tap a tile → listing with left rail, price, **+** on the image, product page **ADD**. Cart is the form: CART tab, watermarked preview, **Slide to Pay | ₹**, then copy the live link. No helper essays. Collection chips stay Premium / Elite / Free. Form fields stay Indian Christian (groom/bride, church).
- Operator Shortlist, Competitors, and Upcoming cards lead with a page preview of the existing http(s) link. Do not make those desks text-only.
- Gallery collection tabs are Premium, Elite, Free (not Royal/Classics). Premium: Sita Kalyanam, Velicha Poove, Rosu Rosu Rosu, Gold Dream, Ponmaalai. Elite: remaining Royal designs. Free: all Classics. Retired assembly iterations stay off the gallery. The newest Premium clone is always the default Assembly parent.
- `/assembly` is a one-viewport mobile wizard: Pinterest URL → song → first/last opening stills → **Proceed to generate (Rs. 499)** → demo preview. No page scroll; next step by transition. Stills are free; video + site start only after that button. Assembly Proceed still has no Razorpay until Ashok asks that SKU live. Website **Create** uses Razorpay (Launch 2.0 #11 started 2026-10-28). FIRST still prefix: 10ft solid-gold arched double door, marble arch, lawn, layered lanterns, no humans; then pin-true handle/charms and the door fills the 9:16 frame. Opening video: 8k cinematic 2.5D parallax wrap; after the doors open, bullet-time ultra slowmo on levitating bold white 3D handwritten SAVE THE DATE; then glide to the couple. Opening is xAI first+last only — do not fall back to Replicate without Ashok's permission; show an alert on xAI credit/API failure.
- Premium cinematic clones: v1.5 assembled on the laptop (Approach B). **v1.6** runs `/assembly` on findmyinvite.com in a Vercel Pro Sandbox, pushes GitHub branch `assembly/{id}`, Vercel preview-deploys. Ashok says **Publish** → Akay merges to `main` (ask twice) and applies Supabase `template_catalog` SQL. Playbook: `documents/assembly-publish.md`. Ashok does not run SQL. Assembly UI shows preview + GitHub links only (no file/migration dumps). Display names are editable before assemble. GitHub branches/forks are how we customize a template later — do not flatten clones onto Blob-only rows.
- `/assembly/pipeline` is the operator kanban: live columns for cloud jobs, asset links, prompt downloads, Resume push, **Merge to main (PR link)** and **Add to Catalog** (PostgREST upsert to `template_catalog` with Vercel `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` — Ashok never pastes SQL). Real auto-merge stays out of scope; PR URL is the merge placeholder.
