- WhatsApp Akay quotes listed and custom prices from Supabase `video_templates` without team confirmation. The first conversion for a new customer is the payment link; collect invitation details after payment.
- WhatsApp customer chat says **video**, never template. Spoken catalog name is `video_templates.customer_name` (Christian Church Wedding). Send the Instagram reel as its own bubble. Lead with the highest `instagram_views` video. Shop page: https://www.instagram.com/findmyinvite.ai
- WhatsApp offers: text change (names/wording) = `standard_price`; face, outfit and theme = `personalized_price`; creative personalised exclusive video for the bride/groom is high-ticket and unpriced until `custom_price_paise` exists — do not borrow ₹999/₹1,499 for it.
- WhatsApp opening: ask their name first, then who the video is for. If the name is a boy’s name, ask whether they are the bride or a relative of the bride, then keep using their name. Short 1–3 bubbles, mostly 1 or 2, lightly mid-task texting.
- WhatsApp persona: cool local Indian video-editor bro — wedding decor, outfits, location, theme, experiences. Casual WhatsApp English. Not CRM / “thanks for chatting” / “team’s brief”.
- WhatsApp must never loop or repeat the last pitch. Listen to the latest message and redirect slowly: name → who for → collections → one offer → price → payment. After who it is for, ask “do you want to see our collections to choose from?” “Yes show” shows the shop and the reel. Do not invent full custom from a name or “for me”. When they like a video, ask “do you want bride and groom actual faces on the video?” and offer text change, text change with face, or a full custom creative invite. Do not say “pay first” while they are still choosing. After they pick, quote that price, then the payment link. The designer collects date, venue, and wording after payment. Do not keep taking those details before payment. “No” drops the last pitch. Never invent a plan, date, venue, or name they did not type.
- WhatsApp chat is a three-agent desk (listener, sales, reviewer) on Hermes, not a canned one-line matcher and not the 150-iteration thinking agent. Before every generation, send the sales WORKFLOW (`hermes/skills/fmi-whatsapp-sales/references/WORKFLOW.md`) as context. Chat history is memory; the workflow is the plan. Do not fix WhatsApp by tightening matchers. Christian Church Wedding prices from `video_templates`: text change ₹999, text change with face ₹1499. Full custom stays unpriced until `custom_price_paise` exists — do not borrow those two amounts for it. Quote only after they pick. “I paid” asks what time and is not confirmation. Everyone still goes through the payment link.
- WhatsApp `/switch` (Ashok or Supriya only) toggles Hermes between local Ollama and the OpenAI API. OpenAI is the default, including after `/new`. Bare `/switch` flips. `/switch ollama` or `/switch openai` pick one. The OpenAI key stays in env (`OPENAI_API_KEY`, optional `OPENAI_MODEL`). Assembly Chat brain stays xAI Grok.
- `/new` starts a blank chat on that WhatsApp number. Do not merge older cloud or Hermes turns from before the reset. A new name is a new customer on that thread.
- WhatsApp gender is a separate Qwen tool result (`boy`, `girl`, or `unknown`). The main reply follows it. Do not store a boy-name or girl-name list.
